      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the volume of the inscribed sphere, we start by identifying the relationship between the cube and the sphere. Since the sphere is inscribed in the cube, the diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube.\n\nGiven that the edge length of the cube is 6 inches, the diameter of the sphere is also 6 inches. Therefore, the radius \\( r \\) of the sphere is half of the diameter:\n\\[\nr = \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nThe formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a sphere is given by:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the radius \\( r = 3 \\) inches into the formula, we get:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( 3^3 \\):\n\\[\n3^3 = 27\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\( 27 \\) into the volume formula:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\times 27\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4 \\times 27}{3} \\pi = \\frac{108}{3} \\pi = 36 \\pi\n\\]\n\nThus, the volume of the inscribed sphere is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{36\\pi}\n\\] cubic inches.",
